{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1114302-the-world-war-i-thread","id":1114302,"title":"The World War I Thread","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-10T15:44:58-07:00","id":1114302,"title":"The World War I Thread","content":"Since World War I is both a popular time period to talk about and looking to be one of the great crossover eras, I thought I'd make this thread to discuss it. <br /> <br /> <b>Goodbye to All That</b>: Vampire. Set in the European and Ottoman Theatres. Focuses on the destruction of the old regimes, the brutality of vampire societies in the trenches, and rise of the Carthians to the height of their power. From <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/61617/Ancient-Bloodlines?affiliate_id=498510\" target=\"_blank\">Ancient Bloodlines </a>&amp; <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/61284/Ancient-Mysteries?affiliate_id=498510\" target=\"_blank\">Ancient Mysteries</a>.<br /> <b>Ruins of Empire: </b>Mummy. Set in the North African and Middle Eastern Theatres. Focuses on the fracturing and decay of the English, French, and Ottoman Empires over the course of the Great War. From <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/178583/Chronicles-of-Darkness-Dark-Eras?affiliate_id=498510\" target=\"_blank\">Dark Eras</a>. <br /> <b>The Master's Tools</b>: Demon. Set on the Eastern Front and Russian Revolution. More of the focus is on the Revolution itself, but that is, of course, triggered by and changes the flow of the War. From <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/207879/Chronicles-of-Darkness-Dark-Eras-Companion?affiliate_id=498510\" target=\"_blank\">Dark Eras Companion</a>. <br /> <b>The Western Front:</b> Werewolf and Geist. Set on the Western Front (thanks, tips). Don't know much yet, but here's the quote from the <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/chronicles-of-darkness-dark-eras-2\" target=\"_blank\">Dark Eras 2 Kickstarter</a>: <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#353535\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Great War displayed humanity\u2019s potential to commit to wholesale, ceaseless slaughter of their own species. In such an era, the Scar tears asunder, and the Beshilu rejoice in the mire of the Western Front. Meanwhile, soldiers who, by every right known to mortals should be dead, stand back up to rejoin the battle \u2014 or fight back against the Reapers stalking battlefields throughout Europe. Now, both werewolves and Sin-Eaters will struggle to coexist, do their duty, and avoid getting caught up in one of history\u2019s deadliest wars.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>So has anyone set a Chronicle in the Great War before? What happened? What other parts of World War 1 would you like to explore? What other gamelines would you like to include? <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T16:39:40-07:00","id":1114311,"title":"","content":"If you want a fantastic crossover setting, Istanbul was divided up and occupied after WW1 in a very similar manner to Berlin after WW2; if you want mortal espionage from Ottoman, Turkish revolutionary, British, French, and Italian agents (to say nothing of the supernatural factions at play), look no further.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T16:53:03-07:00","id":1114316,"title":"","content":"Right off the bat, I'd say it would be cool to play in Sarajevo within the political environment that lead to the Archduke assassination. Or even just the powder keg that was Europe was before the war.<br /> <br /> Also, in Italy you have poets that convince the population to agree going to war with over the top gestures and general patriotic exaltation. A pretty wild moment that will lead to all that idealism to crush against the realities of war. The whole country was not prepared, technologically and culturally, to fight any kind of war against the other big powers of Europe: WW1 put Italy through a crucible that, on one hand, unified the population but, on the other, lead to...certain bad things a few years later.<br /> <br /> I also always have been fascinated by the impact WW1 style of warfare had on the minds of the soldiers, leading to the sort of PTSD that's pretty much a creation of the 20th Century. It, and its early treatments, are an interesting, if dark and grim, topic. Good material for Beast and Changeling, among others.<br /> <br /> Might have more tomorrow, since I probably should go to bed right now","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 07-10-2017, 07:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T00:48:16-07:00","id":1114469,"title":"","content":"I just want to question/point out - Scars are not Werewolf term ( maybe they are from Geist? ), but Wounds are corrupted places of Shadow Realm. Pointing what tsar done in Russia also sounds as 'not one the subject' of the Western Front for this Dark Era.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Re-reading phrase 'Scar tears asunder' I understand it's mean totally different things and have nothing to overthrown Tzar in Russia or Wounds in Hisil. Still, I would point out that this mass killing must spread Maeljinn corruption on to Shadow Realm in those trenches. Hell, whole Great War is surely feeding <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Thurifuge\" target=\"_blank\">Thurifuge</a>, Architect of Violence and<br /> <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Asmodai\" target=\"_blank\">Asmodai</a>, Queen of Wrath.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 07-11-2017, 04:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T01:18:59-07:00","id":1114474,"title":"","content":"WWI has some nice nuance as a setting as you can present the war itself as the ultimate evil as the characters deal with the fallout without one side being in the right and the otherside wholly evil. &quot;Which side were you on?&quot; &quot;The one in the mud&quot; - and all that.<br /> <br /> The more overdone WW2 narratives tend to quickly become more Manichean in nature. The war itself is only evil in that it the manifestation of Axis aggression. Those who oppose fighting in the war are capitulating to fascism, rather than refusing to participate in a senseless clash of Empires using their citizens as cannonfodder (ala WWI). &quot;Sometimes peace is another word for surrender&quot; - and all that. You couldn't have the story of the Christmas Peace in a WW2 setting (not unless it ends with German soldiers defecting to the Allied side). The Allied side is incontrovertibly in the right comparatively - the only way to end the war is the unconditional surrender of the Axis so their regimes can be utterly dismantled.<br /> <br /> That of course may be why WW2 narratives are overdone to the degree they are - because they're morally simpler stories than WWI narratives are. It's a lot easier to talk about how grandpa fought to defeat fascism, than how great grandpa bravely fought in a war over dominance of imperial territories to make a small handfull of people on either side rich at the equal expense of the brutalized soldiers on both sides of No Man's Land.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 07-11-2017, 05:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T05:55:10-07:00","id":1114546,"title":"","content":"I've found it interesting to role-play the people who were heavily invested in the war; I think there's a tendency to simply ignore soldiers agency in the war.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T14:22:22-07:00","id":1114751,"title":"","content":"I've long had a morbid fascination with Ireland during WW1, and the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Easter_Rising\" target=\"_blank\">Easter Rising</a> in particular. Like the Russian Revolution, it's a Demon-friendly environment, but I think it could also be a fascinating setting for a Geist campaign. Mostly thanks to this quote from Padraig Pearse:<br /> <br /> &quot;They think that they have pacified Ireland. They think that they have purchased half of us and intimidated the other half. They think that they have foreseen everything, think that they have provided against everything; but the fools, the fools, the fools! - they have left us our Fenian dead, and while Ireland holds these graves, Ireland unfree shall never be at peace.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13641-mad_maudlin","name":"Mad_Maudlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T18:16:50-07:00","id":1114839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1114302-the-world-war-i-thread?p=1114474#post1114474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That of course may be why WW2 narratives are overdone to the degree they are - because they're morally simpler stories than WWI narratives are. It's a lot easier to talk about how grandpa fought to defeat fascism, than how great grandpa bravely fought in a war over dominance of imperial territories to make a small handfull of people on either side rich at the equal expense of the brutalized soldiers on both sides of No Man's Land.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know, the show Foyle's War did a good job of looking at WWII, especially in the early days, certainly had some moral ambiguity to it from the civilian point of view.<br /> <br /> As for WWI, there's always more than the front lines or the regions everyone thinks about as important to the war. There was military action in Central Africa, high-seas terror thanks to the u-boats, new technologies springing up to make the killing more efficient/win the war faster, and of course the political wheeling and dealing necessary to carry on the war effort for even another week.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T20:51:45-07:00","id":1114892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1114302-the-world-war-i-thread?p=1114839#post1114839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know, the show Foyle's War did a good job of looking at WWII, especially in the early days, certainly had some moral ambiguity to it from the civilian point of view.</div> </div> </div> </div>From a &quot;from the limited perspective of the people on the ground at the time&quot; maybe. But the historic context of the narrative and the full nature of the Third Reich's campaign for Europe and world as already playing out in the territory they controlled is pretty inescapable.<br /> <br /> Admittedly my perspective on '39 may be being colored from my position as an ethnically-Polish Jew.<br /> <br /> And similarly any ambiguity that might stem from an anti-Western Imperialism view of the &quot;co-prosperity sphere&quot; is given lie by Japan's preceding 29 years in Korea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 07-11-2017, 11:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T01:47:44-07:00","id":1114976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1114302-the-world-war-i-thread?p=1114892#post1114892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From a &quot;from the limited perspective of the people on the ground at the time&quot; maybe. But the historic context of the narrative and the full nature of the Third Reich's campaign for Europe and world as already playing out in the territory they controlled is pretty inescapable.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say that's the heart of moral ambiguity. The contrast between the grand morality of a conflict and the individuals lived experience.<br /> <br /> That said, that's another reason for WW1 being a bit easier, the moral ambiguity between soliders fighting on opposite sides of a war is a lot more acceptable than.the moral ambiguity of administrating a ghetto.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T03:10:35-07:00","id":1114998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1114302-the-world-war-i-thread?p=1114976#post1114976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd say that's the heart of moral ambiguity. The contrast between the grand morality of a conflict and the individuals lived experience.<br /> <br /> That said, that's another reason for WW1 being a bit easier, the moral ambiguity between soliders fighting on opposite sides of a war is a lot more acceptable than.the moral ambiguity of administrating a ghetto.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't believe the latter is moral ambiguity. The fact that human beings are very good at rationalizing and convincing themselves they're not evil, no matter what they're doing, does not actually make the actively carrying out genocide less objectively evil. This does admittedly apply in WW1 with regard to the Ottomans/Turks as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T07:40:39-07:00","id":1115088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1114302-the-world-war-i-thread?p=1114998#post1114998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't believe the latter is moral ambiguity. The fact that human beings are very good at rationalizing and convincing themselves they're not evil, no matter what they're doing, does not actually make the actively carrying out genocide less objectively evil.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry I wasn't clearer, I was referring specifically to the Jewish councils set up to run the ghettos, not the Nazis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T14:54:28-07:00","id":1115267,"title":"","content":"Ah, yes, I see your point then. Yes you can certainly find cases of moral conflict over how to survive the worst of circumstances.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T20:44:35-07:00","id":1117573,"title":"","content":"So here are my current thoughts for expansion ideas of the Western Front era, in no particular order:<br /> <br /> In the Great War, the landscape becomes a wasteland that even the Prometheans have difficulty understanding. A new lineage rises from the gases first unleashed in Ypres, and both the living and the Created must wander far from home. <br /> <br /> Men, boys really, and snatched up by the dozens each day during World War 1. Most of it is the work of propaganda, conscription, and the recruiting machine, but the Gentry are at work across the Western Front too. Those Changelings who do manage to make their way back from Arcadia are left wondering if this War is really better than what they left behind as they struggle to create Freeholds in the Trenches and occupied cities. <br /> <br /> Monsters lurk under your bed, at least until the real monsters march into your city. Innocents during the Great War must contend with both no matter which side of the war they are on. France, Britain, Belgium, or Germany... none of them are safe.<br /> <br /> Hunters must march to war while still keeping up the Vigil. Monster hunting is dangerous prospect as it is, but in no-man's land, it's even worse.<br /> <br /> In the shadows and shell craters, darkness breeds and spread. The Infected reach new heights during the war, their occult pathogen hidden within by the other disease ravenging the trenches.<br /> <br /> Vampire is another possibility, especially because I love both of the bloodlines in Ancient Bloodlines, but it is probably an outside possibility since we already know about Vampires during the Great War.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T21:04:44-07:00","id":1117581,"title":"","content":"I think Beast could make well for an expansion to Western Front. What with battlefields and trenches as a lair, gases and shrapnel as environmental conditions, and Beasts themselves being able to personify the horrors of war and become PTSD incarnate for the soldiers present.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5557-runcible","name":"Runcible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5557_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"164"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T00:26:27-07:00","id":1117629,"title":"","content":"Revolution in Russia is a perfect setting for Vampire. Carthians aiding the revolutionary forces and Invctus supporting the loyalists and so on. Circle of the Crone trying to hide under the rock","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12924-orzhov","name":"Orzhov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T13:10:45-07:00","id":1150749,"title":"","content":"And now we can add Promethean into the mix too! I'm pumped and not just because it's my expansion. World War 1 is a perfect time period for Promethean Stories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T17:39:53-07:00","id":1150842,"title":"","content":"Well they are the hollow men.<br /> <br /> So, we all focus in on Europe, the Middle East, and Africa, but what was happening in South America?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-20T14:38:58-07:00","id":1151482,"title":"","content":"Some random ideas:<ul><li>There's some obvious parallels between soldiers coming home with PTSD and Changelings returning form Arcadia to a home where they no longer belong. But they're so strong that you might wonder if you need Arcadia and all things fae at all?</li> <li>You could probably have some Geniuses hanging around the weapons labs, though it would probably work best if you set the game a bit after the war with a bunch of scientists realising that for all their brilliance they were mere pawns in the game of empires and the work did nothing to help, and much to harm, mankind. The game is about how they find closure (or how they fail to find closure).</li> <li>For Hunter: Definitely a time for occult Conspiracies to collapse, or be weakened before WWII finished them off. Groups like America's Freemasons or Victorian occult societies are starting give way to more technological Conspiracies like VALKYRIE. Conspiracies actually fighting in the war feels more WWII than WWI though.</li> <li>You could do a weird but potentially very interesting spin on Deviant with draft dodging, the white feather campaign, and basically replacing Deviant's overt active conspiracy with more subtle omnipresent pressure for society. Or maybe this will work better for Demon, with Covers being civilian identities with good reasons not to get shipped off to the front lines and the government replacing the God Machine.</li> <li>Hunter again: Who takes over the vigil when just about everyone who knows how to fight is a continent away on the front lines?</li> </ul><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-05T21:04:03-07:00","id":1225163,"title":"","content":"I just saw <a href=\"https://www.msn.com/en-us/news/world/the-great-war-pictures-that-are-not-colourised-incredible-photographs-of-world-war-i-taken-by-some-of-the-first-colour-cameras/ss-AAydBUb?li=BBnb7Kz&amp;fullscreen=true\" target=\"_blank\">this link</a> on Facebook and thought it may be useful if anyone is looking to plan a campaign.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-05T22:59:42-07:00","id":1225174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1114302-the-world-war-i-thread?p=1117573#post1117573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In the Great War, the landscape becomes a wasteland that even the Prometheans have difficulty understanding. A new lineage rises from the gases first unleashed in Ypres, and both the living and the Created must wander far from home.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's been an Extempore concept of mine for a while now that I've yet to be able to really use.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-06T03:12:16-07:00","id":1225209,"title":"","content":"There was a horror film I saw, I can't remember its name. But the plot could essentially be summed as the Front becoming such Hell on Earth that it's created its own devils to preside over it. You could use Inferno or the Shadow Realm for that, or core book horrors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-06T11:29:53-07:00","id":1225370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1114302-the-world-war-i-thread?p=1225209#post1225209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There was a horror film I saw, I can't remember its name. But the plot could essentially be summed as the Front becoming such Hell on Earth that it's created its own devils to preside over it. You could use Inferno or the Shadow Realm for that, or core book horrors.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Deathwatch</i>?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2203-corrigan","name":"Corrigan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-06T23:56:56-07:00","id":1225528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Corrigan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1114302-the-world-war-i-thread?p=1225370#post1225370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Deathwatch</i>?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds familiar.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-07T10:42:00-07:00","id":1225623,"title":"","content":"Where would you place a Mage setting during WW1? Seems like an interesting time, the Free Council hasn't yet reached adulthood and the Arrow hadn't yet abandonned championing of Sleeper causes, so they though against each other on both sides.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-08T19:18:32-07:00","id":1226006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Menace</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1114302-the-world-war-i-thread?p=1225623#post1225623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where would you place a Mage setting during WW1? Seems like an interesting time, the Free Council hasn't yet reached adulthood and the Arrow hadn't yet abandonned championing of Sleeper causes, so they though against each other on both sides.</div> </div> </div> </div>What CInder saif about Italy:<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1114302-the-world-war-i-thread?p=1114316#post1114316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, in Italy you have poets that convince the population to agree going to war with over the top gestures and general patriotic exaltation. A pretty wild moment that will lead to all that idealism to crush against the realities of war. The whole country was not prepared, technologically and culturally, to fight any kind of war against the other big powers of Europe: WW1 put Italy through a crucible that, on one hand, unified the population but, on the other, lead to...certain bad things a few years later.</div> </div> </div> </div>... makes me think of Mage. This idealised sense of patriotism and glory vs the grimmer reality sounds like a possible to mirror to the Supernal and the Fallen. Perhaps an early faction of the Free Council supports the war - even in the face of how terrible it is - because they think such a crucible will provoke more Awakenings.<br /> <br /> <b>Beast:</b> One of the most common complains, discussions, and hacks about Beast (coming from many different sentiments) is alternate philosophies to that of lessons. WWI is an era where that could be put front and centre.<ul><li>At the Front the first and most basic interpretation is what the hell Beasts can possibly have to teach among the trenches?</li> <li>Away from the Front, other Beasts may be trying to use the War itself as a lesson: perhaps spreading news about the worst of it, feeding on the reactions, but in the hopes of preventing such a thing happening again; or else they think a big terror some distance away is too much distraction, and people need to be reminded that fear can still find them at home.</li> <li>The War consumes every aspect of life in the nations that fight it. Perhaps Beasts who still regard themselves as altered humans are ascendant in this period, regarding the commonality of experience with the people around them as outweighing their supernature. Maybe some use their Lairs to hide people, or for strategic purposes.</li> <li>Maybe some Beasts convince themselves that their feedings are ultimately a comfort, even to their victims - a personal, psychic fear providing a refuge away from the cold impersonal fear of industrialised warfare.</li> <li>Some would be tempted to say the hell with it. In a world where humans can do that, who cares what Beasts do?</li> <li>And what about Heroes? Do any of them doubt the importance of their quests - who cares about monsters when you're facing the world's first tanks? Or do they believe that killing enough Beasts will end the War? Do they regard the War as a tool to be harnessed? Those good Heroes who aren't indiscriminate about hunting Beasts will surely find a lot to do.</li> <li>And the Dream itself will be roiliing something fierce. New Chambers, new Horrors, new Insatiables by the truckload.</li> <li>And some - some Beasts, Heroes, cultists, or others - will think the War is the Mother feeding for herself...</li> </ul><br /> Overall theme... both Beasts and Heroes, to live themselves, have to work pretty hard at convincing themselves they're right. What happens when the world kicks all that certainty out from under you, and then throws chaos at you to thick and fast to process it.<br /> <br /> <b>Deviant:</b> Deviants are defined by having their souls cracked open. Shell-shock - or some attempt at treating it - seems like something that could do that. In the latter case, where it's a treatment gone wrong, the conspiracy could be motivated by getting people back to the meat-grinder - but they could also be motivated by entirely positive ends - they might even want to help the Deviants, though the Deviants could still be forgived for having had enough of their help. Of course the Trenches are a place to hide from any number of people looking to hunt you down, and where scars may help disguise Scars. And the game will have a strong dichotomy of conviction vs loyalty - the applicability of that to a wartime setting is obvious.<br /> <br /> <b>Hunter:</b> Any of the losing nations could make a good setting for Hunter after the War. The existing order is knocked over, depriving conspiracies of the support networks - both the larger organisations of hunters and those of the monsters they fight will be uniquely vulnerable. That works best for Tier 3 maybe.<br /> The Front itself is good for Tier 1. To quote <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4433_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4433\" data-vbnamecard=\"4433\">Second Chances</a>: &quot;Hunters must march to war while still keeping up the Vigil. Monster hunting is dangerous prospect as it is, but in no-man's land, it's even worse.&quot; (It's also a good way to get hunters from different background and groups taken away from their networks and thrown together).<br /> And for Tier 2, to quote <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar134_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"134\" data-vbnamecard=\"134\">The Kings Raven</a>: &quot;Who takes over the vigil when just about everyone who knows how to fight is a continent away on the front lines?&quot; This is a time when new compacts are needed in every nation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-09T07:50:37-07:00","id":1226076,"title":"","content":"I'm sure it's not unique in it's approach but I think you could get some good material from <a href=\"http://battlefields.ca/product-category/tv-series/\" target=\"_blank\">For King and Empire</a>. Although it focus on the Canadian, you have Norm Christie narrating the events, showing the various Great War cemeteries as well as what the battlefields look like today, but it's intersected with actual footage from the War as well as reading of letter that were sent from the front to family mrmbers in Canada. <br /> <br /> It could help get the mood of life in the trenches.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Project consolidation:<br /> Rough Draft: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1230422-rough-idea-for-a-werewolf-mini-supplement\" target=\"_blank\">Dhole Shifters</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1212511-city-book-seeking-advice\" target=\"_blank\">Ottawa By Night</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1194394-fanon-tribebook-bunyip-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook Bunyip</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=354143#post354143\" target=\"_blank\">Garou Variant</a><br /> In redaction: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1151956-%E1%B9%A3ill%C4%81nu-b%C4%93lu-lasombra-bloodline-feedback-request\" target=\"_blank\">Lasombra Bloodline</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","name":"Boneguard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}